packages/elements/test/node/readme.test.ts:1001: unit-tests: packages/elements/README.md: ocelle-code-block (020) states: **Digests.** An element that shows a digest (a hash, with or without an algorithm prefix) groups it the same way: the prefix is everything up to and including the last colon and is shown as written; the rest is split into groups of four code points from the start, the last group holding the remainder. Units are inline boxes separated by a `<wbr>`, with a `--ocelle-space-1` gap after every unit but the last, so a line never starts with a gap; no character is added, so a copy and the screen-reader reading give the digest as written. Groups do not wrap inside (`white-space: nowrap`, as `-` and `/` in base64 and base64url are break opportunities), so lines break only between units; a prefix that with its gap is wider than the line breaks inside (WCAG 1.4.10). Text holding whitespace is not a digest and is shown ungrouped. `ocelle-code-block`'s `digest` is the first use; `ocelle-facts` values are the consumer's text and are not grouped.: AssertionError: expected '# @ocelle/elements The Ocelle web com…' to contain '**Digests.** An element that shows a …'
